  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>As we know, impulse is the area under the curve of the force vs. time graph. So, analysing each figure area under curve.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>a</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#8208;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>b</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#8208;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>c</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#8208;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>d</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#8208;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math></p><p>From above calculations, area under curve in figure (b) is maximum. Thus, fig (b) impulse is&nbsp;highest.</p>"
